    hero: {
      title: 'PLAIT SOLITAIRE',
      subtitle: 'Card Game',
    },
    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Plait Solitaire',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Plait Solitaire (also known as 'Plaits' or 'The Braid') is a double-deck solitaire game of significant complexity and visual appeal. It is distinguished by the 'Plait'â€”a central reserve of 13 cards arranged in a braid-like pattern, where only specific cards are accessible at any time. Requiring the player to manage two sets of foundations and eight tableau piles, it is a game of foresight, sequence planning, and careful reserve management.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Dates back to the mid-19th century as a complex 'Grand Patience' played in European parlors. The 'Plait' layout was designed to provide a decorative yet difficult reserve element.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'One player. Plait is a solo patience game played by a single person; BVS and historical sources describe it as a single-player card game with no opponents or partners.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '104 cards (two standard 52-card decks).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '104 cards (two standard 52-card decks).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Deal 13 cards in a plait (open reserve). Deal 32 cards into 8 tableau piles (4 cards per pile). Place one card above as the first foundation base; the seven other cards of the same rank become foundation bases as they appear. Remainder is stock.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Standard: Standard Plait: 13-card plait reserve, 8 tableau piles (4 cards each), 8 foundations (one base rank revealed at start), remainder stock; build up in suit on foundations, down alternating color on tableau; no redeal.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Similar games: Braid, Cadonette and Fort are similar double-deck solitaires documented by BVS but are distinct games with their own rules.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Other variants: No other named variants for Plait Solitaire are documented in BVS or primary sources.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
